## Decision and counting rule

Split #4471 into one ticket per cause in the desk's view. Deduplicate by report id, look up the tenant's locale and booking form, and classify using the report channel with the supplied causeOf function. Do not count the original meta.intakeTag guesses as causes. Original labels remain unchanged and are shown only for comparison.

The course's last feedback confirmed the problems but rejected intake's numbers. This revision changes the counting basis to the desk view, not the two problem definitions. The former investigation #3 remains closed. Its five reports belong to parser under the supplied model and are footnoted there, not counted as another cause. The model's assignment is not a claim that every unusual description has been independently reproduced.

<IncidentEvidence />

## Two independent problems

### Parser: day/month text is interpreted month/day

[Issue #1](https://github.com/ldomzalski-allegro/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1) covers the shared parser path for day-first tenants. R-41200 says 7 April became 4 July. This includes app and email reports even when their tenant uses booking-v3, and booking-v2 form reports. The original intake tag does not decide membership.

Proposed remedy: parse according to the tenant convention or use an unambiguous representation. Verify ambiguous date pairs in both directions, invalid dates, affected app/email and booking-v2 paths, and a month-first control. No product fix has been implemented.

The five reports listed in desk-notes.json are counted here and retained as caveats: R-41202 and R-41620 describe a one-day change; R-41209 mentions June; R-41344 gives different days in Lisbon and Toronto; R-41236 says an invite arrived before booking. The supplied desk view footnotes them under parser. Their wording alone does not establish a timezone, daylight-saving or delivery-order cause. Reproduce them before claiming this parser fix covers their symptoms.

### Hint: booking-v3 gives the wrong format instruction

[Issue #2](https://github.com/ldomzalski-allegro/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2) covers the form channel for day-first tenants using booking-v3. It prints MM/DD/YYYY while the form reads input in the tenant convention. Following the instruction can therefore produce a swapped date. This is not fixed by correcting the shared parser alone.

Generate the hint and input convention from the same locale. Test the form at Alder Physio, Copper Studio and Pale Harbour, verifying the date saved as well as the displayed instruction. Use booking-v2 and app/email as controls. Do not assign all reports from a booking-v3 tenant to this cause: the channel matters.

## Original desk view

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The original component and data are preserved. Its “no ticket of its own” label describes the exported desk snapshot, before our issue #2 existed. The displayed cause counts, including the footnote, are the basis of the current ticket memberships.

## Engineering outcome after the export

The [course engineering update](https://hq.mega.dev/challenges/what-it-shows#engineering-update) marks #4471 closed on **5 October 2026**, after the 4 October data snapshot.

- **Parser — FIXED.** The desk reports `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. Close our issue #1 as **completed**.
- **Hint — WON'T FIX.** The desk reports `booking-v3 form retired`. Close our issue #2 as **not planned**, not completed. The misleading hint was not repaired; its form was retired.

These are the course desk's reported outcomes, not fixes implemented or independently tested by this harness. The report counts remain historical totals from the export. Closed reports must not be described as two repaired bugs. Issue #3 stays closed as a superseded investigation; its five ids remain counted once under parser.

## Replace subject-only deduplication

This proposed record replaces the rule in accepted [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) without rewriting its history. The [triage page](/kb/triage/dedupe) is stale; its accepted label does not establish that its subject-only rule remains correct. The [incident page](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue and one fix, while its components reveal two causes.

<DedupeExplorer />

1. Deduplicate export rows by id; one id is one report.
2. Read the body and check the tenant locale, form and channel. Use the desk cause model rather than the browser-based intake guess.
3. Merge reports sharing a cause, not merely matching subjects. Identical subjects can have different causes; different subjects can share a cause.
4. Unknown tenant or unresolved conflicting evidence requires review; do not invent a cause or silently merge into a known one.
5. Preserve provenance, report ids and diagnostic caveats, and review fresh reports before claiming coverage of a fix.

## Received is not merged

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

A batch of merges is not an incident onset. Receipt dates begin in April and the snapshot ends on 4 October 2026; it does not prove reporting stopped afterwards. The support desk covers multiple products. Do not infer a failure rate from the sched-prod population or assign every report to that product without evidence.

## Operations and limitations

Support owns continued review of new reports and classification discrepancies. The course desk's later engineering update reports a parser fix and retirement of the hint's form, as recorded above. This harness has not inspected the production patch or independently verified deployment. The export is not a live feed or a booking-service reproduction environment. Recompute from a new snapshot before relying on counts as current.

